  "description": "This analysis evaluates free tiers from major AI providers. If you're a developer working on a small project, experimenting with AI capabilities, learning prompt engineering, or prototyping an idea before committing to a paid plan, these options give you real access without spending a dollar. The trade-offs are real — but for hands-on exploration, they're more than enough.",
  "scope_note": "Only providers with a genuinely free tier (no payment required) are included. Trials that require a credit card or paid subscription are excluded.",
  "ranking_direction": "most generous free tier (Best) to most restrictive free access (Worst)",
  "conclusion": "For a $0 budget, **Google AI Studio** gives you the most raw capability, while **MiMo Code** gives you the best hands-on coding experience with a frontier model (while the promo lasts). **DeepSeek** offers a genuinely frontier-level reasoning model for free with a massive context window. **Hugging Face** gives you the most variety to explore. Free tiers are ideal for learning and prototyping — just know that trade-offs (latency, rate limits, data privacy) make them impractical for production use.",
